# Mobile-First Design

> **Golden Rule**: Design for mobile first, then scale up

## Breakpoints (Tailwind)

```
sm: 640px   → Small tablets
md: 768px   → Tablets
lg: 1024px  → Laptops
xl: 1280px  → Desktop
2xl: 1536px → Large screens
```

## Correct Pattern

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Mobile first, then scale up
<div className="flex flex-col gap-2 md:flex-row md:gap-4 lg:gap-6">
  <Card className="w-full md:w-1/2 lg:w-1/3" />
</div>

// ❌ WRONG: Desktop first
<div className="flex-row gap-6 sm:flex-col sm:gap-2">
```

## Mobile-First Checklist

- [ ] Is the base layout for mobile?
- [ ] Do breakpoints scale up (`md:`, `lg:`)?
- [ ] Are touch targets ≥ 44px?
- [ ] Is text readable without zoom?
- [ ] Are forms usable on mobile?

## Responsive Components

```tsx
// Adaptive navigation
<nav className="fixed bottom-0 w-full md:static md:w-auto">

// Responsive grid
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">

// Responsive text
<h1 className="text-xl font-bold md:text-2xl lg:text-3xl">

// Responsive spacing
<section className="p-4 md:p-6 lg:p-8">
```

## Touch Targets

```tsx
// ✅ Button with adequate touch area
<Button className="min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px] px-4 py-3">

// ✅ Links with sufficient padding
<a className="inline-block p-3">
```

## Responsive Images

```tsx
<img 
  src={image}
  className="w-full h-auto object-cover"
  loading="lazy"
/>
```
